ahmia-site on FenrirOS
======================

Installed but NOT started. Read this before enabling it.

1. This is only the web front end. Search results come from an Elasticsearch 8 index
   (ahmia-index, filled by ahmia-crawler). Neither Elasticsearch nor the crawler is in the
   repository. Without a reachable Elasticsearch the site shows no results. Set ES_URL,
   ES_USERNAME, ES_PASSWORD and ES_CA_CERTS in /etc/ahmia-site/env.

2. Result filtering is OFF until you supply the term lists. Upstream keeps its eight
   child-safety filter lists (banned_terms_*.map) out of its repository. The setup step creates
   them EMPTY in /etc/ahmia-site/filters/. Format: nginx map lines like
   "~*term" 1;   (see /usr/share/doc/ahmia-site/banned_terms.map.example). An operator who makes
   a public search engine for hidden services should install real lists first.

3. /etc/ahmia-site/env is created at first start with a random SECRET_KEY and SALT. Edit it,
   then:   dinitctl enable ahmia-site
   The site listens on 127.0.0.1:8000 (gunicorn). To publish it as an onion service, add a
   HiddenServiceDir/HiddenServicePort entry to torrc pointing at 127.0.0.1:8000. ALLOWED_HOSTS in
   /usr/share/ahmia-site/ahmia/settings.py lists upstream's own domains; add yours.

4. The SQLite database is /var/lib/ahmia-site/onionAddDatabase.
